{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary (RESOLVED — see resolution note)\n\nSITE: `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py` `run_sweep(tracker)` — the detached-child compaction entry point formerly composed its config root as `repo_root = os.path.dirname(tracker)`, sanctioned `# repo-root-ok:` in the config-root guard (`scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py`) as the ONE deferred CONFIG-ROOT site of the auspicial-friended-merganser class.\n\nCONTEXT: split off from auspicial-friended-merganser (2ec7-be89-9b01-496a), which fixed the 8 clean `dirname(tracker)`-as-config-root sites. `run_sweep` is spawned with cwd == the canonical STORE and inherits only `tracker`; auspicial DEFERRED this site because the detached child needs a DURABLE code root.\n\nIMPACT (milder than the parent's AC#1): on a relocated store (`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` — the deployed MCP topology, store `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, code `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`) `run_sweep` read DEFAULT compaction config (threshold 10, 1800 s horizon) instead of the project's `[compact]` block — folding the right tickets by the WRONG rule. No gate was disabled.\n\n## RESOLUTION — fixed on origin/main by Gerrit 2344 (`c68cc1de3185`)\n\nThis bug is FIXED and MERGED. `c68cc1de3185` (\"Resolve the sweep's code root, not compose it\", Gerrit 2344, carrying `rebar-ticket: 6bf1-326b-7404-4034`) merged with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` and is an ancestor of current `origin/main`.\n\nThe landed fix calls the bare `config.repo_root_or_none()` in the child (`compact_trigger.py` `run_sweep`, `repo_root = _cfg.repo_root_or_none()`), and removes the `# repo-root-ok:` sanction. One resolver covers BOTH supported topologies:\n\n- **Deployment** (relocated store): `REBAR_ROOT` is exported unconditionally and names the provisioned checkout `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`, so the `REBAR_ROOT` arm resolves the real code root.\n- **Local `make worktree`** (co-located store): the git-toplevel arm reads a cwd that `_proc.detached_child_cwd` has already anchored at the canonical store's parent — the durable main checkout, not the ephemeral worktree. `None` (nothing resolved) passes through as the discover sentinel.\n\nThis design has a strictly WIDER correctness envelope than the alternative `dirname(canonical tracker)` fallback once considered here: it is correct when EITHER `REBAR_ROOT` is set OR the cwd is inside the checkout, whereas `dirname(canonical tracker)` regresses the relocated-store + `REBAR_ROOT`-unset + cwd-in-checkout case back to the original bug (measured; see ticket comments). Rejected alternatives in the landed change: threading the resolved root through the spawn contract (re-runs the durability class of bugs 3198/93a9), and `snapshot_repo_root()` (snapshot-only `\".\"` fallback).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (met by Gerrit 2344 / `c68cc1de3185`)\n\n- [x] AC#1 — `run_sweep` resolves the code/config root independent of store location, via `config.repo_root_or_none()`, with no spawn-contract change and no new parameter.\n- [x] AC#2 — On a relocated store with a non-default `[compact]` block, `run_sweep` honours it (RED->GREEN), AND the root it hands `compact_all_cli` IS the resolved code root, pinned at the seam. Config driven by a `rebar.toml` FILE, not env.\n- [x] AC#3 — The `# repo-root-ok:` sanction is removed, leaving the guard allowlist with ZERO deferred config-root sites (only `_store/sync.py`'s store-repo ref reads remain). `python scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py` exits 0.\n- [x] AC#4 — Both precedence arms are exercised, including a test that unsets `REBAR_ROOT` so the git-toplevel arm is covered, not just the deployed arm.\n- [x] AC#5 — A config-effect contrast: the same store/ticket fold NOTHING under a `[compact]` block whose horizon holds the events back, with a LIVENESS check on the sweep's return code (`run_sweep` swallows exceptions, so an absent snapshot would otherwise be satisfied by a crash).\n- [x] AC#6 — Caused-by attribution: same origin class as the parent (`dirname(tracker)`-as-config-root construct), written by `d2dea317ec94` (rebar-ticket `1fde-becd-942a-4351`), recorded as a `caused_by` link.\n\n## Testing (as landed in Gerrit 2344)\n\nThe merged change carries the `run_sweep` fold + seam tests, the `REBAR_ROOT`-unset arm test, the folds-nothing + liveness contrast, and the guard self-test asserting no deferred config-root site; `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the module-size gate and the complexity ratchet stay clean.\n\nNote: an earlier revision of this description (during a parallel remediation attempt) mandated a `compaction_child_repo_root` resolver; that approach was abandoned (Gerrit 2352, ABANDONED) because it would have reverted the strictly-better merged fix. See ticket comments for the full trail."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787959853627622001,"uuid":"f5ebedcf-5c33-4bab-ac67-eb60e489a0cf"}